2... f5 $6 { The Latvian Gambit: Black weakens the king with this pawn move and hopes for tricks. If White keeps calm, the weakened diagonal to e8 is the target. } 3. Nxe5 { Takes the pawn. Black's queen will attack the knight, so d4 comes next to support it. } 3... Qf6 ( 3... d6 4. Qh5+ { Check on the weakened diagonal. } 4... g6 5. Nxg6 { Wins a pawn, and the knight forks the rook on h8 and the bishop on f8. } 5... Nf6 6. Qh4 Rg8 7. Nxf8 ) ( 3... Nc6 4. Qh5+ g6 5. Nxg6 ) 4. d4 { Supports the knight on e5 and takes the centre. } 4... d6 ( 4... Nc6 5. Nc3 ) 5. Nc4 { The knight goes to a safe square where it eyes d6. } 5... fxe4 ( 5... Qg6 6. e5 d5 7. Ncd2 ) 6. Nc3 { Develops and attacks the pawn on e4. } 6... Qg6 7. Ne3 { Covers g2, which the black queen is aiming at, and keeps the extra pawn. Plan: develop the pieces, castle, and watch for ...Bh3 or queen raids on g2. } *
